{"name":"Dainty Lace","hex":"#decfbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dainty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elegant; delicately small and pretty.","Fastidious and fussy, especially when eating."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicacy (choice or pleasing food).","A fancy cookie, pastry, or square, frequently homemade, served at a social event."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dainty"},{"term":"lace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light fabric containing patterns of holes, usually built up from a single thread.","A cord or ribbon passed through eyelets in a shoe or garment, pulled tight and tied to fasten the shoe or garment firmly."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten (something) with laces.","To interweave items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lace","blocks":[{"text":"Lace is a decorative openwork textile made without the use of pre-existing fabric. Lace can be made by hand or machine. Various techniques can be employed to form lace, each having a distinct category. Lace can also be used to refer to other types of openwork fabric such as cutwork or filet, which use pre-existing fabric."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG/330px-Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lace"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/CUR.55.96.123b_view21.jpg/500px-CUR.55.96.123b_view21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/CUR.55.96.123b_view21.jpg/1280px-CUR.55.96.123b_view21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/CUR.55.96.123b_view21.jpg/500px-CUR.55.96.123b_view2